        <p>BAPTIST CHURCH, OOLBORNE STREET, WARRINGTON. SUNDAY NEXT, JUNE 3RD. REV. HERBERT DUNNICO. Morning 10 45. Evening 630. " The re-union of Christendom hindrances." Ordinance of the LorcVs supper at the olose of the Evening Service. ALL SEATS PREF. HEARTY WHLOOMM. METHODIST FREE CHURCH, BUCKLEY STREET, WARRINGTON.—SUNDAY SCHOOL ANNIVERSARY, PARR HALL, WHIT-SUNDAY, JUNE 3RD. Preacher: R. CAMERON, Esq., M.P. Afternoon. at 2,45,, MUSICAL SERVICE, THE APOLLO PRIZE MALE CHOIR. Conductor, Mir. Harry Berrey. Chairman, MR. JOHN UPSON, Speaker, REV. SIDNEY PITT. Special Anthems by the Children and Choir at all Services. livening. at 6.30. Soloist, Miss L. PLINSTON, Organists, Mr. A. E. Trow and Miss M. Plinston, A.L.C.M., Conductor, Mr. N. Cook. MORNING SERVICE at 10 30 in the Church. Preacher, R. CAMERON, Esq., IIP. Colleczions in Aid of the Sunday School.</p>
        <p>COUNTY BOROU(U OF W ARRINGTON.- HORSII PA.RADB. The 6th ANNUAL FARAD&amp; will take place on SATURDAY, JUNE 9m. ALL TURNOUTS i be on the ground at ASPLEY at 11.45 a.m. JUDGING to commence at 12. Any competitor not in his Place at that time will be disqualed. PROCESSION TO START OFF AT 2 P.M. Non-competitors wishing to join in the procession to be in their places, la Slutcbers-lane, by 1.30. A. H. OLIVE, 6. Fgypt-street, Warrington, Hon. Secretary.</p>
        <p>THE REV. HERBERT DUNNICO tHsTimomult FUND. The Rev. Herbert Dunnico closes his ministry in War- rington on the 24th June, 1906. 14 has been suggested that the present would be a fitting opportunity to recognize his services to the town. He has, during the four years of his ministry at Golborne- street Baptist Church, taken a decided stand for the cause of morality and righteousness, and has been untiring in his efforts to promote the social welfare of the people. 1 here are many who have expressed a desire to sh ow their ipprecisticu ot his zeal and sincerity, and they are not by • any means confined to his particular Church. I t. c ol4nti zli sip:rt.:l:e inh. etarasetfibooernee,,w appointed.iibeeni ,e md eacdied eadt tto e emba.kee of publichis lsy i, r To we setii 1- Iflonial to him, and with' that object a Representative Service, to be held in the Parr Hall on Sunday, the 24th I• June, 1906. DAVID GRUNDY (Chairman', 297 Lovely lane. JOS. ELWELL. 227 Liverpool rd., 1. Joint A. P. FREEMAN. 737, Liverpool rd., I Hon. Secs. ..... EDMUND OSB('RER 29,Lovely lane. Hon. Treas., , . LANCASHIRE COUNTY ASYLUM, WINWICK, WARRINGTON. THE COMMITTEE ON VIIITORS INVITH TENDERS for the supply of House Coal and Slack from the lit July next to the 30th June, IEO7. Tenders mus,, be made upon forms which can be obtained from the undersigned, and must be delivered at the Asylum not later than 9 a m. on Wednesday, the 13th June next. The Committee do not bind themselves to accept the lowest or any tender, and reserve to themselves the right to accept Or reject the whole or part of any tender. By order, HENRY ELIAS, Clerk and Steward. •</p>
        <p>29th May. 10;9.</p>
