        <p>LPING THE POLICE.--INTERESTING PRESENTATIONS. 'Mayor of St. Helens (Mr. H. Martin) on Wedncs- 'Ohl behalf of the members of the borough force, Ited silver-mounted walking sticks to Mr. George i of Hard-lane ; Mr. Edward Farelough, 71, New , treet, and Mr. Peter Kay, 48, Barris-street, in ition of services rendered to one of the con- I cof the force. The Chief Constable said that on I nth, two travelling hawkers were drunk and 1g a great disturbance in Hard-lane. Vieben mutable Jon ecs ordered them off, the men ' and badly mauled him, and one of them went 1 scissor-grinding machine and got a thin sharp ; , At this time the other man bad the officer on the ;and it seemed as if the file intended to stab the The three gentlemen named above, however, ' to the assistance of the exhausted officer, and the ll'are arrested after a great melee and were dealt ; I.t the police court. The members of the force ' s'Lesirous of recognising the services rendered to ' -a-constable Jones, for he was no doubt in great when Mr. Maybe stopped the man with the file ' to him. The officer had been kicked about like a 'I, and was unable to do anything fru ther at the one appreciated such assistance more than 'lice did, and every member of the force had con- -1 towards the presentation. The Mvor, in the presentation, warmly commended the for their courlgeous and valuable assistance.</p>
