        <p>- -- DECEMBER, 1905.</p>
        <p>Bessie Miles ... Sarah Fisher Annie Walker ... Lucy Taylor ... Mary Wright ... Mary Malone (.. Annle Bowyer...</p>
        <p>Class. Division. 2 1 , 2 3 2 ;3 2 4 , 2 4 2 5 . 3 1</p>
        <p>..--._ ___ ....__... Mabel Walker... ••• ••• ... 3 . 1 Kate Ford ... ••• ... ... 3 1 Lucy Travis ... ... ••• •-• 3 1 Gertrude Delaney ... ••• ••• 3 2 Elizabeth Hi 11... ... ... ••• 3 2 Marion Oldfield ... —• ••• 3 2 Jessie Whittaker ... ... ..• :3 2 Osborne Sinclair .., ... ... :3 2 May Whittle ... ... ... ... 3 2 Isabella Marshall ... ~. ... 3 3 Kathleen Wainwright .. ... 3 3 Eva Taylor .. ... ... ... 3 3 Ellen Ditchfleld ... ... ... 3 3 Frances Waring ... ' • ... ... 3 4 Edmund Bloor 5</p>
        <p>APRIL, 1906.</p>
        <p>\ Clnss Division. Mary Gandy ... ... ... ... 1 5 Beatrice Alatrobtig ... ... ... 2 1 Ellen Daintith ... ... ... 2 1 Isabel Price ... ... ... .. 2 1 Daisy Nrold ... ... ... ... 2 1 Hilda Davis ... ... ... ... 2 3 Gertrude Farrall ... ... ... 2 3 Margaret Roddy ... ... ... 2 3 May Westwell ... ... ... o -. 3 Teresa Mal one 4</p>
        <p>Lilian Atkinson „. ._ ... 2 5 Mary L. Rislaop ... ... ... 2 5 Frances Jolley .. 9 5 Eva Wood ... ... ... ... :3 1 Mary Marron.- ._ _. -. 3 1 Edith Townley ... ... ... 3 I Teresa Byrne ... ... ... ... 3 ~ _ Edith Crosby ... ... ... ... . 3 ' _ Alfred Crag ... ... ... ... 3 0 _ Elizabeth Duckworth ... ... ' 3 :3 John G. Kenny ... ••• ... 3 William Collins ... ... ... 3 1</p>
        <p>Over many parts of Berwickshire during the lest day of two fosies have been carrying off many lambs,particu. larly on the farms of the Redhenqh, Cockburnspath, and Lammermoor Hill district. This week thirteen foxes have been shot apd several litters of cubs captured.</p>
