        <p>WANTED TO BE LOCKED UP.</p>
        <p>• • ---•- - - • On Tuesday, at Runcofn, a man named Thomas Beres- ford, was committed to the Knutsford Quarter Sessions , on the charge of having broken three panes of glass in the shop window of Messrs. Levi Bros., Bridge-street, doing damage to the extent of £l2. On ti e night of the 20th Police-constable Wynne saw the prisoner kick at the windows, and when asked why he had done it, he replied that he wanted to be locked up, as he had no money.</p>
