        <p>Lori Frames and Side Slip. . Although side-slipping still remains a risk •.attentlant on cycling, under certain conditions. much less is beard and seen of the evil than was the case some years ago. • Eqoal wheds and smaller tyres—the latter .of ncoess•ty pampad birder _have u ndou btedly lessened liand yt, slip, btit ..perhaps. the use of low frames has quit,' as much to do with increased immunity. • Tin, feeling of confidence enjoyed by a rider. who knows that he can place his feet on the gropid should his machine slip from under. him, in conjunction , with ordinary caution, makes an enormous difference in favour of maintaining stability over doubtful surfaces. 077 -•••-ot 141 N: / • ' The New Hudson John o'Groats model is a cycle in which thee clfaracteristics of small wheels and low frame is carried out upon a carefully considered plan, which seems to be meeting with much favour, over 2,000 of this model having been :told since its introduction after Mr..olley's record ride from Lands End to John o'Groats on the first sample machine. The wheels of the John o'Groats model are either 26 in. back and front or when desired 24 in. back and 20 in. front. The smaller wheels enable the frame to be built lighter anfT, at the same time, niore conipaat and stronger. This is an innovation upon the right lines which other manufacturers will probably presently consider when preparing their 1907 models. Novices and the Free Wheel.. A leading road-rider has expressed the opinion. that the free wheel is by no means an 'unmixed blessing to the novice. ,Faults of pedalling that would be betrayed at once on a fixed gear are liable to pass unnoticed with a clutch drive, as no defects of style can retard the machine. To acquire the habit of lifting the feet smartly during the return of the cranks calls for practice on a fixed gear of moderate proportions, and unless some little trouble be taken to master a good style of pedalling at the beginning, a novice may ride for years without attaining that proficiency whieu renders cycling so thoroughly enjoyable. .</p>
