        <p>PENKETH TANNERY. ARNIITAGE &amp; RIGBY. IF. Swift iJ. Bowyer 13. Atkinson 9 B. Green (capt.).... .. ... 15 S. Shave (capt.) 7 T. Rathbone l5, E. Dumbell l5 H. Gilbert 5 I W. Goulden l3 W. Bridge 5 J. H ighatn E. Bond J. Swift J. Lloyd H. Bowyer A. Bowyer 146 128 Majority for Penketh 18 CROFT. 'Re members of the Croft Bowling Club held their opening games on Saturday, on the green attached to the Horse Shoe Inn. Prizes were competed for and some close games ensued, the winners being :—1 , William Maines ; 2, H. Hankinson ; 3,3. Unsworth ; 4, T. Oakes; 5, J. Maines, jun. An excellent knife and fork tea prepared by Hostess Maims having been enjoyed, the prizes were distributed to the successful competitors by Mr. T. Oakes, who presided. The officers for the coming year were elected as follows :—Presi- dent, Mr. T. Oakes • vice-president, Mr. J. Singleton ; secretary, Mr. H. IlLnkinson • treasurer, r. J. Maines In.; committee, Messrs. H. M Shaw, J. Hankinson, S. Taylor, J. Cook, and J. Daintith. An enjoyable smoking concert followed. WARRINGTON JUNIOR CONSERVATIVB CLUB V. CROWN HOTEL, L/mm.—The above teams met on the ground of the latter on Saturday, and an interesting game resulted in a victory for the home team by 38 points-12 on the singles and 36 on the doubles. ST. HELENS MAN KILLED. Williana Gorman (44), living at Parr, St. Helens, died in the Haydock Cottage Hospital on Saturday from injuries received at Messrs. Evans's Parr Colliery. Gorman was a roof repairer and he was knocked down I by a stone falling from the roof on Friday afternoon, and seriously injured internally. FATAL SHOOTING ACCIDENT. A coroner's jury at Niton (Isle of 'Aright) on Wed- nesday returoed a verdict of "Accidental death "in the case of Major Abel Henro Bayley, 6th Manchester IRegiment, who slipped down the steps of the Niton miniature rifle butts on Monday, causing the revolver with which he had been practising to discharge beneath his heart.</p>
